{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"inexistent-tempting-nerka","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# The global rebar build is 4 days stale, and it SILENTLY disables the LLM tier of plan review\n\n## Context / Problem\nThis machine's global `rebar`/`rebar-mcp` is supposed to track `origin/main` HOURLY via a\nrollback-guarded LaunchAgent (documented in `docs/local-env-main-tracking.local.md`). IT HAS NOT RUN\nSINCE 2026-07-27 17:10 — measured from the mtime of\n`/Users/joeoakhart/.local/pipx/venvs/nava-rebar/lib/python3.14/site-packages/rebar/llm/criteria/overlay.py`,\nand corroborated by the venv directory's own mtime. Today is 2026-07-31, so the global build is ~4\ndays behind main.\n\n**THE FAILURE MODE IS SILENT DEGRADATION OF THE REVIEW GATE, WHICH IS WHY THIS IS A BUG AND NOT\nHOUSEKEEPING.** `.rebar/criteria_routing.json` carries `activate` as a DICT (scoped per review type),\nwhich main's overlay parser accepts — `git show origin/main:src/rebar/llm/criteria/overlay.py | grep\n\"must be a list of ids\"` returns NOTHING. The stale global build predates that: its overlay.py DOES\ncontain that check and raises `CriteriaError: 'activate' must be a list of ids, got dict`. Support\nlanded in `f3dbe32b0b` (2026-07-27, \"3ba4: Scope project criteria by review type\") and\n`7f4c650114` (2026-07-28).\n\nMEASURED consequence of running `rebar review-plan <id> --ref HEAD` with the global build in this repo:\n\n    \"llm_ran\": false,\n    \"llm_unavailable\": true,\n    \"llm_error\": \"step 'review@then/assemble' failed: criteria overlay .../.rebar/criteria_routing.json:\n                  'activate' must be a list of ids, got dict\"\n    \"verdict\": \"INDETERMINATE\"\n\nThe command EXITS 2 and emits a sidecar. It does not present as a broken install; it presents as a\nplan that could not be reviewed. The DET tier still runs and reports pass/fail per criterion, so the\noutput looks substantive. An operator or agent reading that verdict would reasonably conclude the\nTICKET is the problem. **No LLM review happened at all.**\n\nThe worktree build parses the same file fine — `registry.effective_criteria('.')` returns 44 effective\ncriteria — so this is purely the stale global install, not a repo defect.\n\n## Why this matters beyond one command\nAGENTS.md already warns to run the repo checkout's build rather than a stale global install, and gives\nthe reason as \"silently ignores newer config keys\". This incident shows the consequence is worse than\nignoring a key: an unrelated-looking INDETERMINATE on the claim gate. Any agent that trusts\n`which rebar` gets it. The MCP server is affected the same way and, per the local docs, will not\nhot-reload.\n\n## Approach\nTwo separable pieces:\n 1. DIAGNOSE why the LaunchAgent stopped. Check `launchctl print gui/$(id -u)/com.navapbc.rebar-dev-update`\n    for its last exit status, and the agent's own log, before forcing a sync. A rollback-guarded updater\n    that silently gave up 4 days ago has its own failure to explain — forcing a sync hides the evidence.\n    Force it only after capturing that state:\n    `launchctl kickstart -k gui/$(id -u)/com.navapbc.rebar-dev-update`.\n 2. MAKE THE STALENESS LOUD rather than silent. A gate run whose LLM tier dies on a CONFIG-PARSE error\n    from the installed build is not the same as an LLM outage, and collapsing both into\n    `llm_unavailable` + INDETERMINATE is what made this cost time. A `CriteriaError` while loading the\n    overlay is a CONFIGURATION fault: it should surface distinctly (its own verdict reason or a loud\n    warning naming the installed build's version), so the reader is pointed at the install rather than\n    at the plan.\n\n## Scope\n- The LaunchAgent / updater: diagnosis first, then a sync.\n- `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/` — distinguish a config-parse failure from an LLM outage in the verdict's\n  `llm_error` / reason surfacing.\n- Possibly a startup or gate-time warning when the running build's commit is far behind the repo's.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] the reason the hourly updater stopped after 2026-07-27 17:10 is recorded on this ticket, captured\n      BEFORE any forced re-sync\n- [ ] the global build parses `.rebar/criteria_routing.json` with a dict-shaped `activate`, evidenced by\n      a `rebar review-plan` run whose output shows `llm_ran: true`\n- [ ] a test asserts an overlay `CriteriaError` raised while assembling criteria is reported distinctly\n      from an LLM outage, so it cannot present as a plain INDETERMINATE\n- [ ] [operator-attested] the verdict text or warning for that case names the INSTALLED BUILD as the\n      suspect, evidenced by the observed output pasted on this ticket","id":"7cbe-57bb-5f39-4628","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Global rebar build 4 days stale: silently disables the LLM tier of plan review"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785562688687670001,"uuid":"a5db8775-eca0-46fd-b40c-4687974c0018"}